From bf4ddad652ac50396b164e6ae018a51da31ac890 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 19:41:01 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] feat(v2): expose passive Avalanche diagnostics in node status

Serialize separate poll, peer and driver diagnostic layers with fixed category names, exact integer counters and nullable tip confidence. Keep overlapping layers separate and preserve unavailable confidence versus numeric zero. Status insertion reads observations without changing protocol policy.

Map actual transport close reasons before removing connections, retaining Unknown when unavailable. Classify definitive application rejection and both activation negotiated-capacity rejections explicitly. Driver ownership continues to deduplicate connection removal and count one cause.

A strict focused regression extracts the actual JSON and close-mapping functions, checks the serialized schema with distinct values and UINT64_MAX round trips, verifies null/zero confidence and nonmutation, and checks Node::Status/rejection source wiring. Independent source review passes. This helper test does not execute whole Node::Status or establish quorum/finality acceptance.
